## 7. Backend: Admin Approval Lifecycle Invalidation

### Fix 7.1: Invalidate Caches Upon Project Approval / Rejection
- **File**: `api/src/services/resources/roadmap-project.service.ts` or Admin Project Service
- **Problem**:
  When a user creates a project (`status: "pending"`) or updates one (`status: "updated"`), it is omitted from public Redis caches.
  When an admin approves the project, if the admin action does not call `roadmapProjectCache.invalidateProjectCaches(slug)`, the public catalogs and roadmap projects tabs will continue serving the old cached list without the new project until the 30m–1h Redis TTL expires.
- **Required Fix**:
  Ensure the admin approval handler calls `roadmapProjectCache.invalidateProjectCaches(slug)` immediately upon approving or status-updating any project.

